From: Project Luma <engineering@projectluma.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Retain the HIDL manager reference before releasing its lock

Waydroid refreshes this shared strong reference for each host/container lookup.
Copy the result while holding the same mutex as the reset. Otherwise concurrent
codec/HAL lookups race a strong-pointer copy against destruction of its pointee.
Keep upstream refresh behavior and transport selection; change no public ABI.
The modified source retains its AOSP copyright and Apache-2.0 license.

--- a/transport/ServiceManagement.cpp
+++ b/transport/ServiceManagement.cpp
@@ -269,9 +269,10 @@ sp<IServiceManager1_2> defaultServiceManager1_2(bool useHostHwBinder) {
                 sleep(1);
             }
         }
+        // Another lookup may reset the shared sp immediately after unlock.
+        // Retain our own reference before releasing the manager mutex.
+        return gDefaultServiceManager;
     }
-
-    return gDefaultServiceManager;
 }
 
 static std::vector<std::string> findFiles(const std::string& path, const std::string& prefix,
